<description>&lt;p&gt;Colombia has opened an embassy in Jerusalem and launched a cultural counterrevolution that is removing more than thirty artworks from the National Museum and ordering the removal of LGBTQ2S+ political works. The Mobile Anti-Riot Squad (ESMAD) has returned to operate in the country and an evangelist was killed after refusing to lend a motorcycle to a criminal group in Cartagena. Former rebel leaders have been charged with war crimes against Indigenous groups, while the president has called for US troops on the ground and linked Colombia's peace process to democratic change in Venezuela. An earthquake in Colombia has left more than 224 dead and rescue operations continue, and a Colombian asylum seeker was tackled by ICE agents outside his home in Washington. 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitAFBVV95cUxNMGZaSTJGM0hWR2ZQa3F5aHVkSjViRVZCY1NGLWhNaHNTQkRUWmFHMGFfckdkVDhfTFJLa2VEcVk4UEx3YWw3ckUwSW1TOXNaTTVETHlrQ1RoR0FlTEZDQUtiU19UeUdBa2dlV1BNU0FUWkVpZzJ6SE1UOVVpVHljWV8wWTZDSWZMdEZ3OEdrWUpYTllRdG1qQmdWd2Y3aXhlOFpCVEdRLTI3ZHpfMFJHQ1JKVEU?oc=5&quot;&gt;globalpost.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Demócrata&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiWEFVX3lxTE5OYWRNYXEzLXdLYjFxZ1BsWEUtSUdqU1o1TU80Nm96eWRLd0w0T2JjNjJkLUxNWm9ENS1xeW1NRllVNmwwLUlVampfOG8zNzhUOGdBblZ5Y2w?oc=5&quot;&gt;CubaHeadlines&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxNVTJubnhqRW12amY5RFlwZnlGb195WTR6TmVBRHhCWk1EUmQ4YjVQNVExVENXNnFyQjB2bWtRODVCQU5WQlhReGlMYTZGTWZjcng4T1ZXOW4zUE83YTlvTTJ2SUFXOFZRcy1JeWxmOTNXb3RxNXFoVjBudVdGSEk1amtWMEx0ZzM3akxiaXl3R1FhaThPUHJManNTWVAtVGV0aERFSXpJTnpxaHYtdm1KMmtzT3NzQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Premier Christian News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;